==Venue==
[[File:Istanbul Atatürk Olympic Stadium 1.jpg|thumb|right|275px|The [[Atatürk Olympic Stadium]] in [[Istanbul]] hosted the final.]]

This was the second UEFA Champions League final played at the [[Atatürk Olympic Stadium]]; the first was held in [[2005 UEFA Champions League final|2005]], when [[Liverpool F.C.|Liverpool]] secured their fifth title after defeating [[AC Milan|Milan]] on [[Penalty shoot-out (association football)|penalties]].<ref>{{cite news |last=Reidy |first=Paul |url=https://en.as.com/soccer/champions-league-final-2023-venue-where-is-ataturk-olympic-stadium-and-what-is-its-capacity-n/ |title=Champions League final 2023 venue: where is the Atatürk Olympic Stadium and what is its capacity? |work=[[Diario AS]] |date=7 June 2023 |access-date=10 June 2023 |archive-date=7 June 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230607192910/https://en.as.com/soccer/champions-league-final-2023-venue-where-is-ataturk-olympic-stadium-and-what-is-its-capacity-n/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Host selection===
{{for|the details on the selection of London as the original host for the final|2024 UEFA Champions League final#Host selection}}

An open bidding process was launched on 22 February 2019 by UEFA to select the 2022 and 2023 UEFA Champions League final venues.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.uefa.com/news-media/news/024e-0f8e68aa43f5-6b3adef08395-1000--9-associations-bidding-to-host-2021-club-finals/ |title=9 associations bidding to host 2021 club finals |website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=22 February 2019 |access-date=14 September 2019 |archive-date=18 June 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200618165213/https://www.uefa.com/insideuefa/about-uefa/news/newsid=2593491.html |url-status=live }}</ref> National associations had until 22 March 2019 to express interest, and bid dossiers had to be submitted by 1 July 2019.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://uk.reuters.com/article/uk-soccer-champions-final/london-mayor-backs-bid-to-host-2023-champions-league-final-at-wembley-idUKKCN1UQ26G |title=London Mayor backs bid to host 2023 Champions League final at Wembley |work=[[Reuters]] |date=31 July 2019 |access-date=14 September 2019 |archive-date=19 September 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200919145455/https://uk.reuters.com/article/uk-soccer-champions-final/london-mayor-backs-bid-to-host-2023-champions-league-final-at-wembley-idUKKCN1UQ26G |url-status=dead }}</ref>

While the bidding associations were not confirmed by UEFA, the [[German Football Association]] was reported to have bid with the [[Allianz Arena]] in Munich, should they not be awarded the 2021 final.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.stuttgarter-zeitung.de/inhalt.allianz-arena-in-muenchen-dfb-kandidiert-auch-fuer-champions-league-finale-2022.175a07bc-e44a-4e6e-9f4a-a01464ca7f7f.html |title=DFB kandidiert auch für Champions-League-Finale 2022 |trans-title=DFB also bids for 2022 Champions League Final |work=[[Stuttgarter Zeitung]] |date=19 March 2019 |access-date=14 September 2019 |language=German |archive-date=18 June 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200618134235/https://www.stuttgarter-zeitung.de/inhalt.allianz-arena-in-muenchen-dfb-kandidiert-auch-fuer-champions-league-finale-2022.175a07bc-e44a-4e6e-9f4a-a01464ca7f7f.html |url-status=live }}</ref> The Allianz Arena was selected by the UEFA Executive Committee during their meeting in [[Ljubljana]], Slovenia, on 24 September 2019,<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/0255-0e99f55f1d05-6273cba59e7c-1000--champions-league-final-hosts-for-2021-2022-2023-and-2024/ |title=Champions League final hosts announced for 2021, 2022 and 2023 |website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=24 September 2019 |access-date=24 September 2019 |archive-date=22 December 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191222151850/https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/newsid=2625232.html |url-status=live }}</ref> where the hosts for the 2021 and 2022 finals were also appointed.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.uefa.com/news-media/news/0255-0f8e6f9636b1-db5308c8e2e5-1000--uefa-executive-committee-agenda-for-ljubljana-meeting/ |title=UEFA Executive Committee agenda for Ljubljana meeting |website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=17 September 2019 |access-date=17 September 2019 |archive-date=18 September 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190918021511/https://www.uefa.com/insideuefa/about-uefa/news/newsid=2623092.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 17 June 2020, the UEFA Executive Committee announced that due to the postponement and relocation of the [[2020 UEFA Champions League final|2020 final]] due to the [[Impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on association football|impact of the COVID-19 pandemic]], Munich would instead host the 2023 edition.<ref name="ExCo 17 June"/> Istanbul had initially been appointed for the 2021 final, but after it was relocated due to the [[COVID-19 pandemic in Europe|COVID-19 pandemic]], they were awarded the 2023 final; Munich would host the [[2025 UEFA Champions League final|2025 final]] instead.<ref name="ExCo 20 July"/>

